WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.000
If you're planning an event, or if somebody just
dropped that responsibility on your lap,

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.200
you know the pressure.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.700
When an event goes great, everybody remembers it.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.500
And when it doesn't, they remember that too.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.200
Finding the right entertainment
isn't just about talent.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.500
You need someone who understands your goals,
can read the room,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.200
and makes you look really smart
for bringing them in.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.700
Before I perform, I want to know
what a win looks like for you.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.000
Do you want your team connecting more,
more energy in the room,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.600
more people stopping at your trade show booth?

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.800
An MC who can keep everything moving
and handle the unexpected?

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.600
Once I know the outcome you're after,
I customize what I do around it.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.900
One client and I had this exact same conversation,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.700
and by the end they decided
my official title should be...

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.800
"CEO of Vibe."

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.000
Honestly, that's still one of the best
descriptions of my job.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.500
The magic is the tool.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.000
The real goal is what happens
to the room because of it.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.700
I've performed thousands of shows in 43 countries,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.500
so I know how to read a crowd, adjust in the moment,

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.800
and make the entertainment fit the event.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.300
[FOX 35 host] This is tremendous.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.100
So tell me what success looks like for you.
I'll help you create it.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.300
And when everyone tells you what an incredible event
you put together,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.400
you get to take the credit for it.
